// QW — a contract from offer to credit.
// Source of truth: protocol/nips/NIP-QW01-job-lifecycle.md (9000-9005) and
// NIP-QW02-credit-issuance.md (9010).
//
// The property worth drawing: no step is atomic. Each one tolerates the other
// party being offline indefinitely — that is the mobile reality the design
// starts from, not a limitation of it. Completion is signed by each side
// separately for the same reason.

title Job lifecycle

Client [icon: user, color: violet]
Worker [icon: user, color: blue]

Client > Worker: 9000 offer\nskill_tags, hours, rate, ko, km, terms

loop [label: "until terms agree — either party, repeatable"] {
  Worker > Client: 9004 counteroffer\nfull replacement set of terms, not a diff\ne tag -> superseded offer
}

Worker > Client: 9001 accept

opt [label: "optional, either party"] {
  Worker > Client: 9002 milestone
}

// Not a handshake: two independent signatures over the same completed work.
// Neither waits for the other, and the record is the pair.
Worker > Client: 9003 completion (worker's signature)
Client > Worker: 9003 completion (client's signature)

Client > Worker: 9010 credit issuance\nQuants = Hours x Rate x ko x km

// ko: objective coefficient (equipment, conditions, hazard).
// km: subjective motivation/quality coefficient.
// Both may be null — negotiation is allowed to stay simple.
